=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/FleetAPI (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/FleetAPI   kind=page   web route=/fleet-api
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/FleetAPIPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's
  idealized "FleetAPIPage.xaml + FleetAPIPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real
  conventions (matching the sibling W7 admin pages ApiLogsPage / VehicleCostPage); the surface registers itself with
  the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("FleetAPI" — RouteTable already maps Page("FleetAPI","fleet-api",AdminDevTools)).
- Data sources bind to the generated C# OpenAPI client (ADR-004) through an IFleetApiFeed seam (P1/S8): four reads
  (get_api_v1_settings, get_api_v1_settings_polling_config, get_api_v1_dev_tools_telemetry_capture_stats,
  get_api_v1_system_version) and two mutations (post_api_v1_settings_suspend_api {suspended},
  put_api_v1_settings_polling_config <full config>). EmptyFleetApiFeed is the headless default; FleetApiClientFeed is
  the contract-client adapter, exercised by ClientFeed_* tests. The web hook names (useSettings, usePollingConfig,
  useCaptureStats, useVersionInfo, useToggleAPISuspend, useUpdatePollingConfig) are preserved at the C# call sites in
  the XML docs of IFleetApiFeed / FleetApiClientFeed. No unit-bearing fields on this admin surface (SI N/A); fmtInt is
  ported through the shared NumberFormatting port.
- 69 new i18n rows (translation.fleetApi.*) added to Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw; common.noData already exists
  verbatim. The surface resolves all 70 manifest strings through the ILocalizer facade with the exact web English
  defaults (the projection records every key — asserted headlessly by FleetAPIPageTests via a RecordingLocalizer in
  both the success and loading states, and the distinct-key count == 70).
- Pre-existing, out-of-scope note: Strings/en/Resources.resw carries a malformed (merge=union) <data
  name="translation.Volume over Time"> element missing its </data> close tag (present in git HEAD; the resw→PRI
  tooling tolerates it — the WinUI build's PRI generation succeeds). Left untouched per scope.

